<title>ALBANIA: EIB gives Albania 12 mln ECU for power station.</title>
<headline>EIB gives Albania 12 mln ECU for power station.</headline>
<dateline>TIRANA 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Investment Bank (EIB) on Friday gave a 12 million ECU ($15.3 million) of credit to Albania to build a new electrical power station and a cable linking two southern towns, an energy ministry spokesman said.</p>
<p>Astrit Karadaku said the three-year credit would be used to build a 220 kilovolts power station in Vlore, 140 km (87 miles) southwest of Tirana.</p>
<p>A 220 kilovolts cable would also be laid down between Vlore and Fier, 100 km (62 miles) southwest of Tirana.</p>
</text>
